<title>USA: High cotton prices trigger import quota - USDA.</title>
<headline>High cotton prices trigger import quota - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>High cotton prices triggered another special quota permitting entry of 44,522,887 kilograms (98,156,244 lbs), U.S. Agriculture Department said Thursday.</p>
<p>The quota, being established Nov 27, applies to cotton purchased no later than Feb 24, 1997, and entered into the United States no later than May 25, 1997.</p>
<p>The quota amount is for August 1996 through October 1996.</p>
</text>
